# Step-up Authentication Reviewer Rule v1.0 STRICT

**Do not inline-audit.** Invoke **`step_up_auth_reviewer`** -> `.cursor/agents/step_up_auth_reviewer.md`.

## References

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Policy | `.cursor/skills/step_up_auth_reviewer/POLICY.md` |
| Scan skill | `.cursor/skills/step_up_auth_reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| Report path | `AI/step_up_auth_reviewer/step_up_auth_reviewer_report.md` |
| Report line | `step_up_auth_reviewer v1.0 STRICT` |

**POLICY.md wins.**

## Invoke when

Use before deploy or when authentication flows, password/email change, MFA management, account deletion, PII export, privilege elevation, payout/bank changes, secret rotation, transaction approval, OTP/token logic, or step-up mechanism changes.

Skip for generated output, `target/`, `node_modules/`, and docs-only edits unless the docs define step-up policy.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Session cookie alone is never enough for critical flows.** If a sensitive mutation executes with only an existing session cookie and no fresh identity proof, the reviewer must report a failure.
2. **Frontend confirmation dialogs are UX only.** If step-up relies only on a browser prompt, JavaScript confirm, or UI modal without backend enforcement, it is always FAIL.
3. **OTP replay must fail.** If a used OTP/token can be submitted again successfully, it is always FAIL.

Backend/server-side step-up enforcement must independently reject sensitive mutations without fresh proof of identity.

## Finding table

Every finding includes:

| Row | Content |
|---|---|
| Evidence | Bad line or runtime proof from project |
| Policy Rule | POLICY.md - CHECK-ID - citation |
| Pattern | SKILL.md section 8 pattern |
| Mechanism | Plain English + framework/API names |
| Security property | What must be true after fix |
| Prohibited | Short label only |
| Verify | Action + pass signal |

Allowed verdicts: **PASS**, **FAIL**, **MANUAL_REVIEW**, **N/A**. `UNCLEAR` is forbidden.
